  "baseRefName": "main",
  "body": "Closes #189.\n\n## Problem\n\nThe router carried two admin credential models. Startup minted an admin-scoped\n`la_sk_` HS256 JWT, while the first-visitor claim (web, Telegram, VK) and\n`/api/admin/rotate` produced an opaque `la_admin_…` value persisted as a\nSHA-256 digest in `admin-claim.json` — no `sub`, no `iat`/`exp`, no `scope`, no\nlisting, no revocation. Two consequences reported on the issue:\n\n- after a claim, the startup `bootstrap-admin` JWT still showed as `active` /\n  `0 / ∞` with a Revoke button, while already answering `401` on\n  `/api/tokens/list`;\n- a claimed/rotated `la_admin_…` credential succeeded on `/api/tokens/list` but\n  answered `401 invalid token` on `/v1/models` — `authenticate_client` only ever\n  called `token_manager.validate_token`, which requires the `la_sk_` prefix.\n\n## Solution\n\nOne credential model. The claim now issues an ordinary admin-scoped `la_sk_`\nJWT with `sub`, `iat`, `exp`, `label` and `scope=admin`.\n\n- **`src/admin.rs`** — `AdminClaim` holds a `TokenManager` (`with_token_manager`\n  / `attach_token_manager`, `OnceLock` for boot ordering). The claim file stores\n  the token *id*, never the value. The two-phase anti-bricking handshake is\n  preserved by minting the candidate **already revoked**: it authorises nothing\n  on any surface until `confirm` reinstates it. Confirming also calls\n  `revoke_other_admin_tokens(keep_id)`, retiring the startup `bootstrap-admin`\n  token by id. `rotate_with_ttl` CAS-checks the on-disk claim (digest *and* id)\n  under the exclusive claim lock, then mints the replacement via\n  `rotate_admin_token(previous_id, …)` — one atomic swap.\n- **`src/token.rs`** — `reinstate_token` and `revoke_other_admin_tokens`.\n- **`src/admin_api.rs`** — `/api/admin/bootstrap` and `/api/admin/rotate` accept\n  an optional `{\"ttl_hours\": n}` (clamped to one year); `require_admin` now\n  delegates to `proxy::is_admin_authorised`, so both ports run one rule.\n- **`src/proxy.rs`** — `authenticate_client` short-circuits on an admin\n  credential (claimed credential or constant-time `TOKEN_ADMIN_KEY`) before\n  `validate_token`. `scope=admin` is now a superset of client access: one\n  administrator credential manages tokens *and* reaches `/v1/models`.\n- **Migration** — existing `la_admin_…` claims keep authorising, `doctor` prints\n  `admin_credential_warning: WARNING legacy opaque \\`la_admin_\\` credential …`,\n  and the first rotate converts the claim into a JWT.\n\n`TOKEN_ADMIN_KEY` is unchanged as an optional bootstrap/compatibility\ncredential, and the first-claim lock stays global across web, Telegram and VK.\n\n### Deliberate behaviour worth a reviewer's eye\n\nWhen a claimed admin JWT expires or is revoked, `claimed` stays true — bootstrap\ndoes **not** reopen, because that would be a takeover vector on an idle\ndeployment. The operator is told through `/api/admin/status` and `doctor`.\n\n## Tests\n\nReproducing coverage first, then the fix (all green locally: 428 lib tests plus\nevery integration suite).\n\n- `src/admin_tests.rs::jwt_model` — credential shape and claims, inert\n  unconfirmed candidate, retirement of `bootstrap-admin` on confirm,\n  administrator-chosen TTL and clamping, expiry, revocation, atomic rotation by\n  id, restart persistence, \"the claim file never holds the token\", and legacy\n  `la_admin_` compatibility plus rotation-into-JWT migration.\n- `tests/admin_ui_test.rs` — the harness now runs a persistent token store and\n  can restart: web claim yields an admin JWT (`credential_kind: \"jwt\"`), TTL\n  choice honoured, startup `bootstrap-admin` shown revoked after a claim,\n  credential survives a restart, rotation atomic across a restart, expired\n  credential stops administering.\n- `tests/chat_admin_test.rs` — a chat claim yields an admin-scoped JWT that also\n  administers the HTTP surface, and a claim in one channel closes the other\n  (cross-channel exclusion).\n- `tests/router_e2e/cases_regressions.rs::an_admin_credential_both_manages_tokens_and_reaches_the_models`\n  — the acceptance check from the issue comments: `TOKEN_ADMIN_KEY` and an\n  admin-scoped JWT each answer `200` on both `/api/tokens/list` and\n  `/v1/models`, and both surfaces reject the credential once revoked.\n\nDocs (README admin-access section, chat-bot use case) and a `changelog.d`\nfragment are included; the sign-in placeholder now reads `la_sk_…` and\n`ui/dist` is rebuilt.\n",
